# {{ display_name }} features and roadmap

This file is the single source of truth for what {{ display_name }} does, what is broken and what is planned, for humans
and AI agents alike. [CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md) records what changed and when; this file records the current
state.

## How to use this file

- **Status** of each item: ✅ done · 🚧 in progress or partial (the note says what is missing) · 🐛 implemented
  with known bugs · ⬜ stub · 📋 planned · 💡 idea · ⛔ blocked · 🔍 needs a check before closing.
- **IDs** (`APP-1`, ...) are stable: never renumber or reuse one. New items take the next free number of their
  area. Use the ID in commit messages, CHANGELOG entries and code `TODO`s (`// TODO(APP-3): ...`).
- Items are grouped by area, what works first, then open items by priority. When finishing work, update the item
  in the same commit: mark it ✅ with a pointer (module, test) and move it up. Obsolete items go to *Dropped and
  superseded* with a one-line reason.

